  "scope": "Native nside=512 Haslam+CMB; full chromatic beam/loading; as-built calibration and common MEPA boxcar for all variants. Point references use the upstream engine's own rotation clock; production uses the pinned FFT-ready sidereal clock. Both periods are recorded without modifying upstream. Linear and PCHIP interpolation are model choices. Noise uses full chromatic I-only power plus separate frozen Moon, loss and voltage/current terms. Per-second covariance is divided by available exposure; zero exposure is unavailable. Bias spectra are exported and assumed calibrated for sky-I ratios. Polarized sky power is omitted from system noise and must be small compared with I for these conditional examples."
